---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="About">
  <div class="pb-12">
    <header class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Made for your kitchen</p>
      <h1 class="page-title mt-2">A home for recipes worth keeping.</h1>
      <p class="page-intro mt-4">Kalorec brings family favorites, weeknight staples, and recipes found online into one collection. Your recipes live as plain files in a private GitHub repo you choose.</p>
      <a href="/how-to-use" class="button-primary mt-6">See how Kalorec works</a>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      <section class="surface-card p-5 sm:p-7" aria-labelledby="save-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Collect</p>
        <h2 id="save-heading" class="section-title mt-3">Save what you cook</h2>
        <p class="muted mt-3 leading-relaxed">Write a recipe or import one from a link. Add a photo and tags, then search your collection when you need it again.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="surface-card p-5 sm:p-7" aria-labelledby="shop-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Plan</p>
        <h2 id="shop-heading" class="section-title mt-3">Shop from your recipes</h2>
        <p class="muted mt-3 leading-relaxed">Gather ingredient lines into a list you can edit, check off, copy, and print. Save it with your recipes for next time.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="surface-card p-5 sm:p-7" aria-labelledby="share-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Share</p>
        <h2 id="share-heading" class="section-title mt-3">Share on your terms</h2>
        <p class="muted mt-3 leading-relaxed">Publish only the recipes you choose to a separate public repo. Visitors can view them on your profile and copy them into their own collection.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <aside aria-labelledby="ownership-heading" class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--sage)] p-5 sm:p-7">
      <h2 id="ownership-heading" class="font-serif text-xl font-bold">Your collection stays yours</h2>
      <p class="muted mt-2 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">Your complete collection and shopping list stay in your private repo. Git keeps earlier versions, including old list contents. Unpublishing removes the current public recipe copy, but Git history and copies made while it was public may remain accessible.</p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Layout>
